[00:00.00]Hello, everyone, and welcome back to Mr. English Channel, where learning English is easy and|大家好，欢迎回到 Mr. English Channel——在这里，学英语既轻松
[00:11.26]fun. I'm Emily.|又有趣。我是 Emily。
[00:13.30]Hello, Emily. Hi, everyone. It's so great to be here hanging out with you all today.|你好，Emily。大家好。今天能和大家一起聊天真好。
[00:18.76]It really is. So how's your week going, Paul?|确实。你这周过得怎么样，Paul？
[00:23.14]Oh, man, it's been a pretty crazy week, honestly. Just running around, getting things done,|哦，老兄，说实话这周挺疯狂的。到处跑、把事情做完，
[00:29.30]working a lot. Yeah, I totally get that. My week's been super busy too. It feels like there's always|工作特别多。是啊，我完全理解。我这周也超忙，感觉总有
[00:37.24]something to do, right? Exactly. But you know, even with all the busy days, everything's going well.|做不完的事，对吧？没错。不过你知道，虽然天天很忙，一切都在往好的方向走。
[00:44.54]I can't complain. That's a great way to look at it. We work hard, we pay our bills, we stay busy.|我没什么可抱怨的。这心态很好。我们努力工作、付得起账单、一直有事做。
[00:51.24]But it actually made me think of a really big question today. Oh, a big question? I like those.|不过这让我今天想到一个很大的问题。哦，大问题？我喜欢。
[00:58.16]What's on your mind today?|你今天在想什么？
[00:59.94]Well, since we're both working so hard this week, I wanted to ask you, is money enough to make you happy?|既然我们这周都这么拼，我想问你：钱，足以让人幸福吗？
[01:08.42]Wow, that's a huge question.|哇，这问题真大。
[01:10.84]And honestly, it's something I think everyone thinks about at some point in their life.|说实话，我觉得每个人一生中某个时候都会想这个问题。
[01:15.42]Right?|对吧？
[01:15.72]We spend so much time trying to earn it, but we rarely stop to ask if it's actually doing the job.|我们花那么多时间去挣它，却很少停下来问：它真的起作用了吗？
[01:23.50]And you know, if you guys listening stick around to the end of our chat today,|另外，如果你们今天听到最后，
[01:28.28]you're going to completely change the way you talk about life, success, and happiness in English.|你们谈论人生、成功和幸福的英语方式会彻底改变。
[01:35.22]For sure.|当然。
[01:36.44]You'll pick up so many natural ways to express your deep feelings,|你会学到很多自然地表达深层感受的说法，
[01:40.32]which is so important when you're making real friends in English.|这在用英语交真朋友时特别重要。
[01:44.30]Exactly.|正是。
[01:45.32]So let's just jump right into it.|那我们直接开始。
[01:48.20]I think there's this big illusion in the world today.|我觉得当今世界有一个很大的幻觉。
[01:52.10]An illusion?|幻觉？
[01:53.00]You mean like a trick or something we believe that isn't totally true?|你是说像一种错觉，或者我们相信但其实并不完全真实的东西？
[01:57.38]Yep, exactly.|对，正是。
[01:58.88]The illusion is that once we finally have enough money or success or fame, we'll finally be happy.|这个幻觉就是：等我们终于有了足够的钱、成功或名声，我们就会幸福。
[02:07.70]Oh, yeah.|哦，是啊。
[02:08.38]I hear that all the time.|我总听到这种说法。
[02:10.26]People say, if I just had a million dollars, all my problems would disappear.|人们说：「只要我有一百万美元，所有问题都会消失。」
[02:16.12]Right.|对。
[02:16.92]And we should be fair here.|这里我们得公平一点。
[02:19.54]Money does have a very good side.|钱确实有很好的一面。
[02:21.84]It's not evil.|它本身不是坏东西。
[02:23.00]No, not at all. We need it to survive. It's really nice to go to the grocery store and just buy what you want to eat.|对，完全不是。我们需要它生存。去超市想买什么就买什么，感觉很好。
[02:31.26]Exactly. It provides food, it pays the rent, and it helps us take care of our families.|正是。它提供食物、付房租，也帮我们照顾家人。
[02:37.64]Yeah, and it lets us do fun things, too, like traveling or buying nice gifts for people we love, or sending our kids to a good school.|对，它还让我们能做有趣的事，比如旅行、给爱的人买礼物，或者送孩子上好学校。
[02:46.76]For sure. When you don't have enough money to pay your basic bills, life is incredibly stressful.|当然。当钱不够付基本账单时，生活会压力山大。
[02:53.26]It really is. So having enough money absolutely reduces those daily worries. It gives you a sense of safety.|确实。所以有足够的钱确实能减少日常焦虑，给你安全感。
[03:01.06]It does. But the problem starts when money becomes the only goal.|是的。但问题出在——当钱变成唯一目标的时候。
[03:06.22]Right. When we forget about everything else and just focus on the bank account.|对。当我们忘了其他一切，只盯着银行账户。
[03:11.76]Yeah, I've known people who work so much that they never actually see their families.|是啊，我认识一些工作太多、几乎见不到家人的人。
[03:18.58]I know people like that, too.|我也认识这样的人。
[03:20.40]They work weekends, they miss dinner with their kids, and they ignore their friends.|他们周末上班，错过和孩子的晚餐，也忽略朋友。
[03:25.38]And they usually ignore their own health, too.|而且通常也忽略自己的健康。
[03:28.38]They sleep poorly, they're always stressed out, just to get a bigger paycheck.|他们睡不好，总是压力很大，只为了多拿一点工资。
[03:34.30]It's sad, really, because they're building all this wealth, but they have no one to share it with.|说实话挺可悲的，因为他们积累了这么多财富，却没人可以分享。
[03:39.58]Exactly. So the real challenge is finding the right balance, right?|正是。所以真正的挑战是找到合适的平衡，对吧？
[03:45.12]Definitely. You need financial stability, but you can't forget to actually live your life and enjoy a sunny afternoon.|当然。你需要经济上的稳定，但也不能忘了真正去生活，去享受一个阳光明媚的下午。
[03:53.34]I love how you said that. Enjoying a sunny afternoon doesn't cost anything, but you have to be free to enjoy it.|我喜欢你这句话。享受一个晴朗的下午不花一分钱，但你得有空去享受。
[04:02.88]Yeah, and that brings us to the reality of the situation.|对，这就说到了现实。
[04:07.34]The reality is often very different from the illusion.|现实往往和幻觉差得很远。
[04:11.60]It really is. Just look at the news or read about famous people.|确实。看看新闻，或者读读名人的故事。
[04:16.84]Right. There are so many millionaires and celebrities who have everything we think we want.|对。有那么多百万富翁和名人，拥有我们自以为想要的一切。
[04:23.40]But inside, they're dealing with so much pain.|但内心却在承受巨大的痛苦。
[04:26.94]They struggle with anxiety, depression, and just feeling totally alone.|他们在焦虑、抑郁和彻底的孤独中挣扎。
[04:32.38]It's true. They can buy any house in the world, but they don't have peace.|真的。他们能买下世界上任何一栋房子，却没有安宁。
[04:38.46]Sometimes they fall into bad habits or addictions just to hide the pain.|有时他们染上恶习或成瘾，只是为了掩盖痛苦。
[04:43.74]Which completely proves that money doesn't automatically equal a happy heart.|这完全证明了：钱并不自动等于一颗快乐的心。
[04:49.50]Not at all. And on the flip side, you see people who live very simple lives.|完全不是。反过来，你也会看到生活非常简单的人。
[04:54.46]Yes, people who don't have big houses or fancy cars, but they have these huge, real smiles.|对，他们没有大房子、好车，却有着大大的、真实的笑容。
[05:02.38]I saw this a lot when I was traveling a few years ago.|几年前旅行时，我见过很多这样的场景。
[05:06.30]People living in small villages, sharing simple meals.|住在小村子里的人，分享简单的饭菜。
[05:10.12]And they were genuinely happy, weren't they?|他们是真的快乐，对吧？
[05:13.10]They really were.|真的是。
[05:14.42]They laughed so loudly.|他们笑得那么响亮。
[05:16.32]They helped their neighbors, and they just had this beautiful peace about them.|他们互相帮忙，身上有一种很美的安宁。
[05:21.20]It's so beautiful to see.|看着真美好。
[05:23.84]They have true gratitude for whatever they have today.|他们对今天所拥有的一切都怀着真诚的感恩。
[05:28.00]Exactly.|正是。
[05:28.88]So, it makes you wonder, why does this happen?|所以你会想：为什么会这样？
[05:32.38]Why are the rich people sometimes so sad and the poor people sometimes so joyful?|为什么有钱人有时那么悲伤，而穷人有时那么快乐？
[05:39.24]I think it comes down to understanding the difference between pleasure and happiness.|我觉得归根结底是要理解「快感」和「幸福」的区别。
[05:45.52]Oh, that's a really good point. Pleasure and happiness are definitely not the same thing.|哦，这说得太好了。快感和幸福绝对不是一回事。
[05:52.04]Not at all. Pleasure is very temporary. It's a quick feeling.|完全不是。快感非常短暂，是一种转瞬即逝的感觉。
[05:57.64]Like eating a huge bowl of chocolate ice cream.|就像吃一大碗巧克力冰淇淋。
[06:01.00]It feels amazing for about 10 minutes.|大概十分钟里感觉棒极了。
[06:05.12]Right. Or buying a brand new phone.|对。或者买一部全新的手机。
[06:08.70]You feel so excited when you open the box.|拆开盒子时你兴奋极了。
[06:11.90]Oh yeah, you play with it all day.|哦对，你会玩一整天。
[06:14.74]But a week later, it's just a phone.|但一周后，它就只是一部手机。
[06:17.46]The excitement is totally gone.|兴奋感完全消失了。
[06:20.44]Exactly. Money can buy a lot of pleasure.|正是。钱能买到很多快感，
[06:23.74]It buys the ice cream, the phone, the fancy vacation.|能买冰淇淋、手机、豪华假期。
[06:28.98]But happiness is different.|但幸福不一样。
[06:30.98]Happiness is a lasting feeling.|幸福是一种持久的感觉，
[06:33.24]It's a deep sense of purpose.|是深层的意义感。
[06:35.70]Right.|对。
[06:36.50]Happiness stays with you even when things get difficult.|即使处境艰难，幸福也会一直陪着你。
[06:40.42]Pleasure disappears the second a problem shows up.|而问题一出现，快感立刻消失。
[06:44.18]That's so true.|太对了。
[06:45.64]You can't buy deep, lasting satisfaction.|深层、持久的满足感是买不到的，
[06:48.84]You have to build it from the inside.|你得从内心把它建立起来。
[06:51.26]For sure.|当然。
[06:51.96]And speaking of building good things, if you guys are enjoying this deep conversation today, make sure to hit the like button right now.|说到建立美好的东西，如果你们喜欢今天这场深入的对话，现在就点个赞吧。
[07:01.32]Yeah, and don't forget to subscribe to the channel and share this video with a friend who's learning English too.|对，别忘了订阅频道，并把视频分享给也在学英语的朋友。
[07:06.86]We love growing this community with you.|我们很喜欢和大家一起把这个社区做大。
[07:10.18]In fact, leave a comment below and tell us what makes you genuinely happy in your daily life.|也请在下面留言，告诉我们日常生活中什么让你真正快乐。
[07:16.44]We always read your comments and it's so inspiring to see your answers.|我们每一条留言都会看，你们的回答特别鼓舞人。
[07:21.18]It really is. So, if money only buys temporary pleasure, what actually matters for true happiness?|确实。那么，如果钱只能买来短暂的快感，真正决定幸福的是什么？
[07:30.08]That's the million-dollar question, right? I think the very first thing is peace of mind.|这就是那个「百万美元难题」了，对吧？我觉得第一件事是内心的安宁。
[07:36.98]Oh, absolutely. Peace of mind is priceless. If you lay your head on your pillow at night and feel calm, you're richer than most people.|哦，绝对。内心安宁是无价的。如果晚上躺下时你能感到平静，你比大多数人都富有。
[07:46.46]It's so true. Knowing that you're living honestly and doing your best gives you that peace.|太对了。知道自己活得诚实、尽力而为，就会带来这种安宁。
[07:52.56]And what else? I think good relationships are right at the top of the list.|还有呢？我觉得良好的人际关系排在第一位。
[07:57.86]100%. We're humans. We need connection. We need people to love and people who love us back.|百分之百。我们是人，需要联结。需要去爱别人，也需要被别人爱。
[08:05.22]Exactly. Having someone to call when you have good news or when you're crying.|正是。有好事时有人可以打电话，难过哭泣时也有人可以打。
[08:10.88]Right. Money can't buy a loyal friend. It takes time and care to build real trust.|对。钱买不到忠诚的朋友。真正的信任需要时间和用心去建立。
[08:17.74]And another big one is health. We forget about it until we get sick, right?|另一个重要的就是健康。我们总是病了才想起来，对吧？
[08:22.78]Oh, yeah. When you're healthy, you have a thousand dreams. When you're sick, you only have one dream.|哦对。健康时你有一千个愿望，生病时你只有一个愿望。
[08:28.94]Wow. That's a powerful way to say it. Health is true wealth.|哇，这话说得太有力量了。健康才是真正的财富。
[08:33.12]You can't enjoy anything if your body is falling apart.|身体垮了，什么都享受不了。
[08:36.96]So true. And tied to relationships is just having time with your family.|太对了。和人际关系紧密相关的，就是陪伴家人的时间。
[08:43.66]Yes. Playing with your kids, sitting on the porch with your parents, just talking.|对。陪孩子玩，和父母坐在门廊上聊聊天。
[08:50.30]Those are the moments we remember when we get older, not the extra hours at the office.|这些才是我们老了以后会记得的时刻，而不是在办公室多待的那几个小时。
[08:56.00]Exactly. And I think another big part of happiness is serving other people.|正是。我觉得幸福的另一个重要部分，是帮助他人。
[09:02.36]Oh, definitely. Helping someone else is actually one of the fastest ways to feel better yourself.|哦，当然。帮助别人，其实是让自己心情变好最快的方式之一。
[09:08.46]It's amazing how that works. When you take the focus off yourself and help a neighbor, your own problems feel smaller.|这真神奇。当你不再只盯着自己，去帮帮邻居，你自己的问题就显得小了。
[09:16.68]Yeah, it gives you a reason to wake up. It gives you a purpose for living.|对，它给你醒来的理由，给你活着的意义。
[09:21.20]Purpose is so important. Without it, you just feel lost no matter how much money you have.|意义感太重要了。没有它，不管有多少钱，你都会觉得迷失。
[09:27.12]You know, thinking about purpose and peace, for me, real peace comes from my faith in Jesus Christ.|你知道，说到意义和安宁，对我来说，真正的安宁来自我的信仰。
[09:34.48]I know people have different beliefs, and I respect that, but my relationship with Christ gives me hope, purpose, and peace, even during difficult times.|我知道人们信仰不同，我尊重这一点。但这份信仰给了我盼望、意义和安宁，即使在困难时期。
[09:44.08]I appreciate that perspective, Paul.|我很感谢你分享这个视角，Paul。
[09:46.76]Even if people have different beliefs, I think many of us are searching for the same things.|即使信仰不同，我觉得很多人追寻的是同样的东西：
[09:52.04]Peace, love, hope, and a meaningful life.|安宁、爱、盼望，以及有意义的人生。
[09:56.26]Exactly. We're all looking for that anchor, that thing that keeps us steady when life gets crazy.|正是。我们都在寻找那个「锚」，那个在生活失控时让我们稳住的东西。
[10:02.56]We really are. And it's so nice to talk about these deep things because it shows how English can connect us on a human level.|确实是。聊这些深刻的话题真好，因为它展现了英语如何在人的层面上把我们连起来。
[10:11.04]For sure. You know, we've used some really great words today while talking about all of this.|当然。你知道，今天聊这些的时候，我们用到了不少很好的词。
[10:16.28]We have. There are a few words that just keep popping up naturally in this conversation.|是的。有几个词在对话里不断自然地出现。
[10:21.98]Yeah. Like earlier, you used the word illusion.|对。比如刚才你用了「illusion」这个词。
[10:25.32]I think that's such a helpful word for everyday life.|我觉得这个词在日常生活中特别有用。
[10:28.04]It really is.|确实。
[10:30.16]An illusion is basically a false idea or a trick.|「Illusion」基本上就是一个错误的观念，或者一种错觉，
[10:34.84]Something that looks real but isn't.|看起来真实，其实不是。
[10:37.60]Right. Like thinking a big house automatically fixes a broken marriage.|对。比如以为一栋大房子就能自动修复破裂的婚姻。
[10:42.96]That's an illusion.|那就是幻觉。
[10:44.10]Great example.|好例子。
[10:45.80]Another word we talked about a lot was balance.|我们聊得很多的另一个词是「balance」。
[10:49.50]Oh, balance is everything.|哦，平衡就是一切。
[10:51.64]It just means having the right amount of different things in your life.|意思是生活里各种事情都要有恰当的分量。
[10:55.32]Yeah, like balancing your job and your free time.|对，比如平衡工作和空闲时间。
[10:58.78]You don't want too much of just one thing.|你不希望某一样占得太多。
[11:02.34]Exactly.|正是。
[11:03.32]If you only work, you crash.|只顾工作，你会垮掉；
[11:05.64]If you only play, you can't pay rent.|只顾玩，你付不起房租。
[11:08.16]You need balance.|你需要平衡。
[11:10.58]Spot on.|说得太准了。
[11:12.06]And then we contrasted two really important words, temporary and lasting.|然后我们对比了两个很重要的词：temporary 和 lasting。
[11:17.92]Temporary is such a good word.|「Temporary」是个好词，
[11:20.14]It means something only lasts for a short time.|意思是只持续很短的时间。
[11:23.24]Like a summer rainstorm or the excitement of buying new shoes.|比如夏天的阵雨，或者买新鞋时的兴奋。
[11:27.90]It's temporary.|它是短暂的。
[11:29.20]Right.|对。
[11:29.94]But we want things that are lasting.|但我们想要的是持久的东西，
[11:32.42]Things that stay with us for a long, long time.|能陪我们很久很久的东西。
[11:35.16]Like a strong friendship.|比如牢固的友谊。
[11:37.20]That's lasting.|那是持久的。
[11:38.40]Exactly.|正是。
[11:39.00]And the final word that really stood out to me today was purpose.|今天最让我印象深刻的最后一个词是「purpose」。
[11:43.72]Purpose is your reason for doing something.|「Purpose」是你做某件事的理由，
[11:46.74]It's the why behind your life.|是你人生背后的那个「为什么」。
[11:49.18]Yeah, your job might give you a paycheck, but your purpose gives you energy.|对，工作也许给你薪水，但意义感给你能量。
[11:53.56]I love that.|我喜欢这句。
[11:55.14]When you have these words in your pocket, it's so much easier to have real deep chats with native speakers.|把这些词装进兜里，和母语者进行真正深入的交流就容易多了。
[12:02.12]It really is.|确实。
[12:03.22]But, you know, sometimes it's not just about knowing the words.|不过你知道，有时候光知道单词还不够，
[12:07.52]It's about putting them together naturally.|还要能把它们自然地组合起来。
[12:10.04]Oh, absolutely.|哦，绝对。
[12:11.92]Sometimes I hear people use the right words, but the sentence just feels a little stiff.|有时我听到人们用对了词，但句子就是有点生硬。
[12:18.28]Yeah, like it came out of a textbook instead of a real conversation.|对，像是从教科书里蹦出来的，而不是真实对话。
[12:23.68]Exactly.|正是。
[12:24.96]Like, if someone wants to say that wealth doesn't create joy, they might say,|比如有人想说「财富不能带来快乐」，可能会说：
[12:29.98]I have very much money, but I am sad.|「I have very much money, but I am sad.」
[12:34.10]Right.|对。
[12:34.64]We understand what they mean, but it sounds a little robotic.|我们能明白意思，但听起来有点机械。
[12:38.82]It does.|确实。
[12:39.58]A much more natural native way to express that is simply saying, money doesn't buy happiness.|更自然的母语说法很简单：「Money doesn't buy happiness.」
[12:46.74]Yes, money doesn't buy happiness.|对，「Money doesn't buy happiness.」
[12:49.64]It's an idiom, but we use it literally all the time in everyday life.|这是个习语，但我们在日常生活里真的天天都在用。
[12:53.92]We really do.|确实。
[12:55.34]Here's another one.|再来一个。
[12:56.76]Someone might say, I work all time for money and I am very tired.|有人可能会说「I work all time for money and I am very tired.」
[13:02.32]Again, totally understandable.|同样，完全能理解。
[13:04.44]But a native speaker would probably say, I'm working myself into the ground.|但母语者大概会说「I'm working myself into the ground.」
[13:09.48]Ooh, that's a good one.|哦，这句好。
[13:11.20]Working myself into the ground.|「Working myself into the ground.」
[13:13.36]It paints such a clear picture of exhaustion.|这句话把疲惫感画得太清楚了。
[13:16.66]It really does.|确实。
[13:17.94]It shows you're working so hard that it's actually hurting you.|它表明你工作太拼，已经伤到自己了。
[13:22.36]Definitely.|绝对。
[13:23.40]And what about when someone wants to talk about liking their quiet, normal life?|那当有人想说自己喜欢安静的普通生活呢？
[13:28.14]They might say, I like my simple life very much.|他们可能会说「I like my simple life very much.」
[13:32.92]That's okay, but you'll sound much more natural if you say,|这也可以，但这样说会自然得多：
[13:36.42]I really enjoy the simple things in life.|「I really enjoy the simple things in life.」
[13:38.78]I love that phrase. I enjoy the simple things in life. It sounds so warm and relaxed.|我喜欢这个说法。「I enjoy the simple things in life.」听起来温暖又放松。
[13:46.92]It really does. It makes people feel comfortable talking to you.|确实。它让人跟你说话时觉得舒服。
[13:51.20]For sure. It's amazing how just changing a few words makes the whole feeling of a sentence change.|当然。只改几个词，整句话的感觉就变了，真神奇。
[13:58.26]It totally does. You know, I bet if we put all of this into a real-life situation, it would make perfect sense.|确实如此。你知道，我敢说，如果把这些放进真实场景里，就完全说得通了。
[14:05.28]Oh, definitely. Let's imagine two friends talking at a coffee shop. One of them just got a huge job offer.|哦，当然。想象两个朋友在咖啡馆聊天，其中一个刚拿到一份很好的工作邀请。
[14:13.58]But there's a catch, right? The job pays a ton of money, but it requires crazy hours.|但有个条件，对吧？薪水很高，但工作时间长得离谱。
[14:20.16]Exactly. I'll be the friend who got the offer, and you can be the friend giving advice.|正是。我演拿到 offer 的那个，你演给建议的那个。
[14:25.88]Sounds good. Let's do it. So, Emily, I heard you got that new job offer in the city.|好。开始吧。那么 Emily，我听说你在城里拿到了一份新工作。
[14:31.84]I did. The salary is amazing. I'd be making double what I make now.|是的。薪水很诱人，是我现在的两倍。
[14:37.48]Wow, that's incredible. Are you going to take it?|哇，太厉害了。你打算接受吗？
[14:40.52]I don't know. The money is great, but they want me to work almost 70 hours a week. I'd never be home.|我不知道。钱是很好，但他们要我每周工作将近 70 小时。我根本回不了家。
[14:48.36]Oh, wow. That's a lot. You really have to think about the balance.|哦，哇，太多了。你真得考虑一下平衡。
[14:52.12]I know. I'm worried it's an illusion. Like, I'll have all this money, but no time to actually spend it.|我知道。我担心这是个幻觉：有了这么多钱，却没时间花。
[14:59.56]Exactly. Money doesn't buy happiness if you're working yourself into the ground every single day.|正是。如果每天都把自己累垮，钱买不来幸福。
[15:04.72]You're right. I really enjoy the simple things in life, like weekend hikes and dinners with my family.|你说得对。我真的很享受生活里简单的事，比如周末徒步、和家人吃晚饭。
[15:13.74]Yeah. A big paycheck gives you temporary excitement, but your health and your family are lasting.|对。高薪给你短暂的兴奋，但健康和家人是长久的。
[15:21.10]That's so true. I think my peace of mind is worth more than that salary.|太对了。我觉得我的内心安宁比那份薪水更值钱。
[15:27.06]I agree completely.|我完全同意。
[15:29.28]You have to follow your purpose, not just the money.|你得追随自己的意义感，而不只是钱。
[15:33.06]Thanks, Paul.|谢谢，Paul。
[15:33.94]That really helps me see things clearly.|这真帮我把事情看清楚了。
[15:37.70]And scene.|卡！
[15:39.14]That was perfect.|太完美了。
[15:40.08]It felt just like a real chat between friends.|就像朋友之间的真实聊天。
[15:44.10]It really did.|确实。
[15:45.60]And notice how naturally all those deep concepts just flowed right into the conversation?|注意到那些深刻的概念多么自然地融进对话了吗？
[15:52.02]Yeah.|是啊。
[15:52.54]Yeah, when you stop trying to sound like a textbook, your English just feels so much warmer.|对，当你不再努力说得像教科书，你的英语就温暖多了。
[15:58.64]Exactly.|正是。
[15:59.80]Well, we've talked about a lot of big things today, from crazy work weeks to finding true peace.|好，今天我们聊了很多大话题，从疯狂的工作周，到寻找真正的安宁。
[16:07.02]We really covered a lot of ground.|确实涵盖了很多内容。
[16:09.24]I hope it gave everyone listening something good to think about.|希望它能给每位听众一些值得思考的东西。
[16:13.60]Me too.|我也是。
[16:14.52]Before we go, please make sure you subscribe to the channel, leave a like, and drop a comment below.|结束之前，请务必订阅频道、点赞，并在下面留言。
[16:21.56]Yes, keep practicing your English with us every single week.|对，每周都和我们一起练英语。
[16:26.02]We absolutely love being part of your learning journey.|我们非常喜欢参与你们的学习旅程。
[16:29.76]So as we wrap up today, we want to leave you with one final thought to reflect on.|今天收尾之际，我们想留给你们一个值得思考的问题：
[16:35.50]Yeah, if someone gave you unlimited money tomorrow, would it solve your deepest problems?|如果明天有人给你无限的钱，它能解决你最深的问题吗？
[16:42.08]Or would you still be searching for something more?|还是你依然在寻找更多的东西？
[16:45.24]Think about that.|想一想吧。
[16:46.50]Thank you so much for joining us today, everyone.|非常感谢大家今天的收听。
[16:49.72]See you next time.|下次见。
[16:50.80]Bye everyone.|大家再见。
[16:52.00]Take care.|保重。
